{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Provide for yourselves, etc.</b> He said <b>for yourselves</b> to give the reason of the phrase ״for your tribes״ in advance, for this is beneficial to you when each tribe has its judges from among itself. And see what I wrote in parashat Pinḥas on the verse ״יִפְקֹד HaShem אֱלֹהֵי הָרוּחוֹת אִישׁ עַל הָעֵדָה״ etc. (Numbers 27:16), and there you will understand the nature of the benefit there is in this matter, and that is his saying ״for yourselves״." "<b>And I will set them, etc.</b> Meaning: although I say to you ״provide for yourselves״ — that you are the ones choosing them — they will not be subject to your authority and approval; I will set them as heads over you to rule you with rod and strap."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:14.629079962Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}